OL,3,AVeteran Nigerian Nollywood actor Pete
OL,4,AEdochie dies aged 79
OL,5,
OL,6,FVeteran Nigerian actor Pete Edochie,
OL,7,Fone of Africa's most celebrated film
OL,8,Fstars, has died at the age of 79, his
OL,9,Ffamily has announced.
OL,11,FKnown for his deep voice, commanding
OL,12,Fscreen presence and memorable use of
OL,13,FAfrican proverbs, Edochie became a
OL,14,Fhousehold name across Africa, often
OL,15,Fportraying powerful traditional rulers,
OL,16,Fwealthy businessmen and family
OL,17,Fpatriarchs.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,164,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11915
SC,0015
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1795605893
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AVeteran Nigerian Nollywood actor Pete
OL,4,AEdochie dies aged 79
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn a statement, his family said Edochie
OL,7,Fdied in the early hours of Wednesday in
OL,8,Fthe south-eastern Nigerian city of
OL,9,FEnugu following a prolonged battle with
OL,10,Fprostate cancer.
OL,12,FTributes are pouring in from fans and
OL,13,Ffellow actors, remembering him as a
OL,14,FNollywood legend who helped shape
OL,15,FNigeria's film industry.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG15/19
